conditional rendering:
conditional rendering means based on condition what react should display

if /else
ternary operator
&&

Using if...else
function userProffile({user})=>{
    if (!user){
        return <h1> please login </h1>
    }
    
    return <h1> welcome{user.name} </h2>

}

//ternary

function app(){
    const isloggedin = True;


return(
    <div>
    {isloggedin = True ?(<h1>welcome</h1>):(<h1>please login</h1>)}
    </div>
) 
}

The syntax is:

condition ? trueValue : falseValue

For example:

isLoggedIn ? <Dashboard /> : <Login />

// &&
Using &&

If you only want to show something when a condition is true:
func app(){
    const isadmin = True;
    return(
       <div>
       {isadmin && <button>Delete User</button>}
       </div>
    )
}